WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.730
flag first marks selected categories. scatter counts earlier keep flags to obtain an exclusive offset, then writes the original token ID t.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.770
Both kernels are launched in order in the same stream.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:19.120
This small reference counts earlier flags directly; the model explains the scan-based construction.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.840
Flag tokens.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.305
Record whether each token survives.

00:00:24.305 --> 00:00:26.270
Count earlier survivors.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.935
Form an exclusive destination offset.

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:30.140
Scatter IDs.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.175
Write each selected token once.

00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:38.610
Flags produced in device memory must be ready before scatter consumes them.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.345
Unique offsets give selected threads distinct destinations.

00:00:42.345 --> 00:00:47.780
Stable output order follows the offsets, not the order in which warps happen to run.
